WEBVTT

00:01.282 --> 00:04.763
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV♪

00:04.807 --> 00:08.115
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values♪

00:08.158 --> 00:11.118
♪ On which we used to rely?♪

00:11.161 --> 00:14.556
♪ Lucky there's a family guy♪

00:14.643 --> 00:17.863
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do♪

00:17.907 --> 00:19.474
♪ All the things that make us♪

00:19.517 --> 00:20.562
♪ Laugh and cry♪

00:20.562 --> 00:26.046
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy!♪

00:31.703 --> 00:33.444
Well, here we are.

00:33.488 --> 00:35.446
Time for everyone
to get new shoes.

00:35.490 --> 00:36.926
Hi. Can I help you
find something?

00:37.013 --> 00:38.580
What's she gonna do?

00:38.667 --> 00:40.234
This place doesn't even
have a back room.

00:40.321 --> 00:41.974
All the inventory's
just out on the floor

00:42.018 --> 00:43.802
in ceiling-high library stacks.

00:43.802 --> 00:46.240
Yup, we got it, Stewie.
You're better than this place.

00:46.327 --> 00:48.807
Yeah, I know that.
I'm better than every place.

00:48.894 --> 00:51.332
Yes, my son needs
a new pair of shoes.

00:51.375 --> 00:53.029
Okay, let's just
see what his size is.

00:54.813 --> 00:56.902
Looks like a ten and a half.

00:56.946 --> 00:59.079
They're perfect. I'll take 'em.

00:59.122 --> 01:01.385
No, those aren't the shoes.

01:01.429 --> 01:04.780
[robotic]: Do not speak
in that tone to the Iron Giant.

01:04.823 --> 01:07.522
Must destroy shoebox city.

01:08.827 --> 01:10.960
Sorry.
He's a little out of sorts.

01:11.003 --> 01:13.832
He saw a bra in the window
of Lane Bryant on the way over.

01:13.832 --> 01:15.834
They're, um...
they're pretty big.

01:15.834 --> 01:18.185
They are a remarkable feat
of engineering.

01:18.228 --> 01:21.013
That and the Ferris wheel
I will never understand.

01:21.057 --> 01:22.754
Yeah, for me, it's paper bags.

01:22.798 --> 01:24.713
I mean, there's a door
in it, but no exit?

01:24.756 --> 01:26.976
-What's that about?
-[laughs]

01:27.019 --> 01:28.804
I was serious about the bag,
but, hi.

01:28.847 --> 01:30.240
-I'm Brian.
-Holly.

01:30.284 --> 01:32.634
Holly... are you free
on Friday night?

01:32.634 --> 01:34.505
Well, I don't know.
Are you a shoe store murderer?

01:34.549 --> 01:36.551
N-N-No.

01:36.594 --> 01:38.292
There's more than you'd think.

01:38.379 --> 01:40.642
Like, if you were me, that's not
a ridiculous question.

01:40.642 --> 01:41.991
See you Friday.

01:42.078 --> 01:43.949
Good for you, Brian.

01:43.993 --> 01:45.821
Maybe you can take her
to the Cheesecake Factory.

01:45.864 --> 01:46.952
People seem to like that place.

01:48.302 --> 01:50.130
Did you folks find something
on the menu you'd like?

01:50.173 --> 01:54.090
No. 110 pages, and no.

01:54.134 --> 01:56.701
♪

02:04.013 --> 02:05.754
-What's all this?
-Oh, hey, guys.

02:05.797 --> 02:08.104
Uh, sadly, my Uncle Ray
passed away last week,

02:08.191 --> 02:10.628
but he left me
his vintage sports car.

02:10.672 --> 02:13.109
Joe, that's amazing
that your uncle died.

02:13.196 --> 02:15.285
But I'm really sorry
to hear about the car.

02:15.329 --> 02:17.113
He means that
the other way around.

02:17.113 --> 02:19.333
Uncle Ray also left
strict instructions

02:19.333 --> 02:21.117
for me to show his car
at the Classic Car Show

02:21.161 --> 02:22.814
in Providence this weekend.

02:22.858 --> 02:24.338
Classic Car Show?

02:24.338 --> 02:25.774
Isn't that one
of those gatherings

02:25.817 --> 02:27.776
of a bunch of guys
whose penises don't work?

02:27.819 --> 02:30.822
Correct. Anyone with
a perfectly-restored classic car

02:30.866 --> 02:32.520
for sure has a bum wiener.

02:32.563 --> 02:34.304
Uh, he also left me
everything I'd need

02:34.348 --> 02:38.178
to convert my garage
to a 1950s-style diner.

02:39.527 --> 02:43.139
See, here are all the 1950s
Coke signs from the 1980s.

02:46.186 --> 02:48.318
Oh, cool, and a jukebox!

02:48.362 --> 02:50.277
Yeah, but since the songs
are from the '50s

02:50.277 --> 02:52.235
they're all about men
in their 40s

02:52.279 --> 02:54.150
wanting to have sex
with teenagers.

02:54.150 --> 02:57.153
♪ I wanna...
be-bop a teeny bopper♪

02:57.153 --> 02:59.329
♪ At the sock hop♪

02:59.373 --> 03:02.158
♪ Or maybe after work
behind the malt shop...♪

03:02.245 --> 03:03.855
[new 1950s song intro begins]

03:03.855 --> 03:07.946
♪ 13 candles♪

03:07.946 --> 03:11.123
♪ Is probably enough...♪

03:11.167 --> 03:13.909
♪ Nine, ten, 11-year-old,
12-year-old sex♪

03:13.952 --> 03:16.607
♪ I'm gonna sleep
with all the kids tonight!♪

03:16.651 --> 03:18.827
Joe, stop pressing buttons.

03:18.870 --> 03:21.960
[Somethin' Stupid"
playing in distance]

03:22.047 --> 03:23.962
♪ And then I go
and spoil it all♪

03:24.049 --> 03:26.182
♪ By saying somethin' stupid♪

03:26.226 --> 03:29.664
♪ Like "I love you."♪

03:29.707 --> 03:31.187
[scattered applause]

03:31.187 --> 03:33.363
Boy, I forgot
how great that song is.

03:33.407 --> 03:35.931
I know, right? It's definitely
my favorite romantic love song

03:35.974 --> 03:37.498
sung by a father
to his daughter.

03:37.541 --> 03:38.760
Ooh, we should
put in our next song.

03:38.760 --> 03:40.370
Good thinking.

03:40.414 --> 03:42.329
Yes, we'd like
to request "Witchcraft,"

03:42.372 --> 03:44.635
as arranged
by Mr. Nelson Riddle.

03:44.679 --> 03:45.897
[sighs]
Okay, give me a minute.

03:45.897 --> 03:47.769
You should just know

03:47.856 --> 03:49.379
there's a 21st
birthday party here,

03:49.423 --> 03:51.338
and you're ruining it for them.

03:53.992 --> 03:55.777
Wow.
3:00 a.m.

03:55.777 --> 03:58.170
We practically
shut the place down.

03:58.214 --> 04:01.086
And quite a night.
We got to sing two songs.

04:01.130 --> 04:03.001
Do you mind if I kiss you?

04:03.088 --> 04:05.787
Actually, I should
chew some gum first.

04:05.787 --> 04:07.136
I had bologna for dinner.

04:07.223 --> 04:08.920
Get over here.

04:08.964 --> 04:10.661
[both moaning]

04:12.750 --> 04:14.578
Oh, yeah,
that's good kiss bologna.

04:18.234 --> 04:20.323
Oh, hey, guys,
what's the word?

04:20.367 --> 04:23.152
Uh, bird.
Bird is the word.

04:23.195 --> 04:24.980
But we were wondering
if you'd take us

04:25.023 --> 04:26.373
for a spin in your new car.

04:26.373 --> 04:28.244
Yeah, that's a great idea.
Hop in.

04:30.986 --> 04:34.816
Vroom! Vroom!
Vroom! Vroom!

04:34.903 --> 04:38.298
[imitates clicking,
engine revving]

04:38.341 --> 04:41.431
[imitates gear shifting]

04:41.475 --> 04:43.215
Uh, what-what...
what's happening right now?

04:43.259 --> 04:46.349
Close your eyes, gang, as we hit
the Kancamagus Highway.

04:46.393 --> 04:48.046
Just four miles
to Mount Washington.

04:48.046 --> 04:49.352
What the hell
are you doing, Joe?

04:49.396 --> 04:51.267
We want to go for a real drive.

04:51.354 --> 04:53.269
This isa real drive.
Just imagine it.

04:53.313 --> 04:55.663
Feel that New Hampshire air.

04:55.706 --> 04:57.969
Joe, we're not in New Hampshire.
We're in your driveway.

04:58.013 --> 05:00.189
Oh, great, some knucklehead
is tailgating us.

05:00.189 --> 05:01.973
What's the hurry, pal?

05:02.060 --> 05:05.107
Oh, I see so many birds.

05:05.150 --> 05:07.196
Well, we're in a tunnel, so I'm
not sure how that's possible.

05:07.196 --> 05:09.285
Joe, stop this car right now.

05:09.372 --> 05:11.679
-The car is stopped.
-[imitates gears grinding]

05:11.722 --> 05:13.637
[sighs] Always have trouble
finding third.

05:13.681 --> 05:15.726
[imitates brake squeaking]
Okay, what's up?

05:15.770 --> 05:18.076
You got this amazing car.
Why can't we take it out?

05:18.076 --> 05:19.643
Well, ever since I was nine,

05:19.687 --> 05:21.079
I've dreamed
of driving this car someday.

05:21.166 --> 05:22.994
But I'm not allowed.
It's in my uncle's will.

05:23.038 --> 05:24.605
Even when I take it
to the car show,

05:24.648 --> 05:26.171
I have to put it up
on a trailer.

05:26.215 --> 05:28.173
Malcolm in the Middle,
five nights a week

05:28.217 --> 05:30.741
on Manchester's Channel 12.

05:30.785 --> 05:32.177
Cleveland, stop reading
fake billboards.

05:32.221 --> 05:34.266
Now if you'll excuse me,

05:34.310 --> 05:38.793
I'm off to taste the delights
of downtown Nashua.

05:38.836 --> 05:40.272
I don't care what Joe says.

05:40.316 --> 05:42.405
This is too nice a car
not to drive it.

05:42.449 --> 05:45.277
Are you suggesting we take it
out without telling Joe?

05:45.321 --> 05:46.888
He's left us no choice.

05:46.888 --> 05:49.107
I can't just sit in a car
and pretend to drive,

05:49.194 --> 05:50.892
like-like I had to pretend
to be impressed

05:50.892 --> 05:53.416
by Quagmire's
new big, green grill.

05:53.460 --> 05:55.375
This is the largest
high-performance

05:55.418 --> 05:57.333
ceramic cooker available, Peter.

05:57.377 --> 06:00.205
-NSF Certified.
-Ah, yeah, cool.

06:00.249 --> 06:02.338
I'm starving. When do we...
when do we fire this thing up?

06:02.338 --> 06:05.515
[laughing]:
Fire-fire this thing up?

06:05.559 --> 06:08.126
Get a load of this guy.
You don't just fire it up.

06:08.126 --> 06:09.867
You slowly bring it
to temperature.

06:09.911 --> 06:11.303
[sighs]
Okay.

06:11.347 --> 06:12.870
When do we put the burgers on?

06:12.914 --> 06:15.482
B-B-Burgers?
Are you hearing this?

06:15.525 --> 06:19.094
You don't put burgers on a grill
of this quality, Peter.

06:19.137 --> 06:21.357
I've been brining a heritage
breed chicken for three days.

06:21.401 --> 06:23.577
[sighs]
Then can we put that on?

06:23.577 --> 06:25.492
Yes. At midnight,
when it's reached temperature.

06:25.492 --> 06:27.494
Then why am I here now?

06:27.537 --> 06:30.235
Because I need your help
to move the grill a single inch.

06:30.279 --> 06:32.281
[both grunting]

06:33.848 --> 06:36.154
[sighs]
Well, let's just listen to music

06:36.154 --> 06:38.330
on my high-end stereo system.

06:38.374 --> 06:40.115
Nice.
Let's crank it.

06:40.158 --> 06:42.291
[laughing]:
C-C-Crank it?

06:42.334 --> 06:43.814
You hear this clown?

06:43.858 --> 06:45.294
I only use it
to listen to podcasts.

06:45.381 --> 06:47.470
MAN:
Today onThe Moth,

06:47.514 --> 06:50.473
how a single pair of shoes
reunited two sisters.

06:56.000 --> 06:58.089
So, big date, huh?

06:58.133 --> 07:00.135
You must really like this girl.

07:00.178 --> 07:03.486
Honestly, I think
Holly could be... the one.

07:03.530 --> 07:06.794
Brian, you strike me
as a very selfless lover.

07:06.837 --> 07:09.492
Is that true?
Are you a selfless lover?

07:09.536 --> 07:11.625
Stop saying "selfless lover."

07:11.625 --> 07:13.409
Have you been reading
Lois' romance novels again?

07:13.496 --> 07:15.367
A few,
but I'm just saying I bet

07:15.411 --> 07:18.980
your coital congress will send
Holly into paroxysms of ecstasy.

07:18.980 --> 07:21.417
-Knock it off.
-What? I'm being supportive.

07:21.417 --> 07:23.071
After all,
confidence will help you

07:23.114 --> 07:25.639
maintain optimal stamina
during your lovemaking.

07:25.639 --> 07:27.641
-That's enough.
-Have it your way, Brian.

07:27.641 --> 07:31.862
I myself am a student
of the pleasures of the flesh.

07:31.906 --> 07:34.865
[slurping]

07:36.519 --> 07:39.479
Listen to your lover, Brian.

07:45.310 --> 07:47.008
[stomach gurgling]

07:47.008 --> 07:48.226
Ugh, damn it. Anxiety dump.

07:48.270 --> 07:50.533
[stomach gurgling]

07:50.577 --> 07:53.449
-[unzips]
-Ah, that's better.

08:03.590 --> 08:06.941
Oh, uh, is-is Holly here?

08:06.984 --> 08:09.552
You must be the new jerk
my mom is dating.

08:09.596 --> 08:11.162
Uh, and you must be the kid

08:11.162 --> 08:12.555
she never told me about.

08:16.690 --> 08:19.040
I host Family Guyrepeats
in Germany.

08:19.127 --> 08:20.781
GERMAN ANNOUNCER: German
Family Guy is brought to you

08:20.824 --> 08:23.261
by rail-thin men
in Internet pornos going,

08:23.348 --> 08:25.176
"Ooh-aah, ooh-aah, ooh-aah!"

08:32.009 --> 08:34.359
I'm sorry I never
told you I had a son.

08:34.403 --> 08:35.578
Some guys get scared off.

08:35.622 --> 08:37.362
No, no, that-that's great.

08:37.406 --> 08:39.060
I'm-I'm terrific with kids.

08:39.060 --> 08:40.496
I actually have a kid.

08:40.496 --> 08:42.716
Aw, that's sweet.
How old is he?

08:42.716 --> 08:45.196
Uh, I don't know.
How long ago was Ratatouille?

08:45.240 --> 08:46.850
Well, I'm gonna
go finish getting ready.

08:46.894 --> 08:49.200
Why don't you guys get
to know each other a little?

08:54.728 --> 08:58.296
So, uh, is there a dad that you
spend weeks of your time with?

08:58.340 --> 09:00.472
My dad moved to Florida.

09:00.516 --> 09:03.519
Sounds right. What, um...
what grade are you in, bud?

09:03.519 --> 09:05.652
-Second.
-You don't say.

09:05.695 --> 09:07.654
Boy, I bet things are different
than they were in my day.

09:07.654 --> 09:09.873
Lot of school shootings now.

09:09.917 --> 09:12.006
-What?!
-Oh, no. No, no, I...
No, I just meant...

09:12.049 --> 09:14.182
Like-like, people
bring guns to school?

09:14.225 --> 09:15.575
What? No, no,
I'm-I'm not saying...

09:15.618 --> 09:17.446
And they just shoot kids?!

09:17.489 --> 09:19.187
Well, you can hide
under your desk.

09:19.230 --> 09:21.624
The desks won't be enough!
[crying]

09:21.668 --> 09:23.713
All set.
You guys getting along?

09:23.757 --> 09:26.324
Yup, just great. All right,
let's go eat at a waffle house,

09:26.411 --> 09:28.936
and then I'll show you
all my bow-hunting carcasses.

09:28.979 --> 09:30.894
That sounds like
a perfectly normal date.

09:33.941 --> 09:35.725
♪

09:41.644 --> 09:43.341
Okay, I got a perfect way

09:43.428 --> 09:45.517
to distract Joe
while we take his car.

09:45.561 --> 09:49.217
There's literally
no phone survey he won't take.

09:49.260 --> 09:51.088
-[phone ringing]
-Hello?

09:51.132 --> 09:52.568
Yes, Joe Swanson?

09:52.612 --> 09:54.526
On a scale of one to ten,

09:54.570 --> 09:57.138
how happy are you
with your Wi-Fi service?

09:57.138 --> 10:01.751
Well, I'd say it's Wi-Fine.
[chuckles]

10:01.795 --> 10:03.144
I came up with that
ten months ago

10:03.231 --> 10:05.537
in anticipation
of this very call.

10:05.581 --> 10:07.409
Ha. Terrific.
And would you be willing

10:07.452 --> 10:09.454
to take a half-hour survey

10:09.498 --> 10:12.501
in your far upstairs bedroom
while facing the wall?

10:12.544 --> 10:15.069
Also, how loud does your TV get?

10:15.112 --> 10:17.375
BONNIE:
Don't be long, Joe!
I'm expecting a call.

10:17.419 --> 10:19.508
I'll take the time I need!

10:19.595 --> 10:21.728
This is the Wi-Fi call.

10:21.728 --> 10:24.165
[engine starts]

10:24.165 --> 10:26.428
Great job
hot-wiring the car, Cleveland.

10:26.471 --> 10:28.299
The key was in the ashtray,

10:28.343 --> 10:31.172
but your presumption
will not be forgotten.

10:31.172 --> 10:32.869
[engine revving]

10:38.919 --> 10:41.748
[sighs]
You know, you're the Cub Scout.

10:41.791 --> 10:44.272
We're supposed to be making this
Pinewood Derby car together.

10:44.315 --> 10:45.752
I don't care.

10:45.795 --> 10:49.625
Hey, you're one kid,
and we're four kids,

10:49.625 --> 10:51.714
-so we're gonna bully you.
-[grunts]

10:51.758 --> 10:53.107
Knock it off.

10:53.150 --> 10:54.674
Or what,
Kyle-Kyle-Dog-Poop-Pile?

10:54.717 --> 10:56.980
Hey, guys?
Let's take it easy

10:57.024 --> 11:00.549
and maybe not use canine feces
as a taunt. That's hurtful.

11:00.549 --> 11:02.420
What?
[chuckles]

11:02.507 --> 11:05.206
He's just saying
that Kyle's a little baby

11:05.293 --> 11:08.296
who's too stupid to even know
how to stand up for himself.

11:08.339 --> 11:10.733
What are you
gonna do, baby-- cry?

11:10.777 --> 11:12.126
-[growling]
-[screaming]

11:12.169 --> 11:14.302
Let go of me!
Stop!

11:14.345 --> 11:15.782
-You're crazy!
-You leave him alone!

11:15.782 --> 11:17.784
[barking]

11:19.133 --> 11:21.657
Whoa.
Thanks, Brian.

11:21.657 --> 11:24.312
Nobody's ever stood up for me
like that before.

11:24.355 --> 11:26.618
Well, I think my instincts
just kicked in.

11:26.662 --> 11:28.446
Want to help me sand your car?

11:28.446 --> 11:30.579
Yeah.
Definitely.

11:33.321 --> 11:35.105
Animal control?

11:35.105 --> 11:38.369
I'd like to schedule
an emergency neutering.

11:38.369 --> 11:40.371
♪

11:42.896 --> 11:45.246
Man, I can't get over
how old-timey

11:45.333 --> 11:46.638
everything in this car is.

11:46.682 --> 11:48.640
I know.
Check out what's on the radio.

11:48.684 --> 11:50.642
NEWSWMAN:
President Kennedy has been shot.

11:50.686 --> 11:53.123
NEWSMAN 2:
The martians are now
traveling to New Jersey.

11:53.167 --> 11:55.125
MAN:
♪ Beatles song, Beatles song♪

11:55.169 --> 11:57.911
♪ La, la, la, la, la.♪

11:57.998 --> 12:00.217
Ah, that last one
brings back a lot of memories.

12:00.261 --> 12:02.176
Wow, this baby
handles like a dream.

12:02.219 --> 12:04.221
Do you guys mind
if I drive with my knees

12:04.265 --> 12:07.703
while I make some last-minute
fantasy football changes?

12:07.747 --> 12:09.052
-Look out!
-[tires screeching]

12:11.359 --> 12:13.927
-Oh, my God!
-Holy crap!

12:14.014 --> 12:16.277
Aw, man,
Joe is gonna be so pissed.

12:16.364 --> 12:18.496
Thank God all we hit
were those trash cans.

12:18.496 --> 12:20.411
Oh, my God.
Oscar!

12:23.675 --> 12:27.375
[grunts]
Tell my ex-wife...

12:27.418 --> 12:29.420
to go [bleep] herself.

12:30.421 --> 12:32.510
Very on-brand.

12:32.510 --> 12:34.208
Right up to the end.

12:39.256 --> 12:41.432
Thank you so much for having
Kyle and me over for dinner.

12:41.476 --> 12:43.391
Everything is delicious,
Mrs. Griffin.

12:43.434 --> 12:45.828
Well, I wasn't sure
what a divorcée eats,

12:45.872 --> 12:47.525
so I just assumed fried things.

12:47.569 --> 12:49.266
No, that's perfect.

12:49.310 --> 12:52.139
What about this guy? Did he help
with any of the cooking?

12:52.182 --> 12:54.228
Brian is not allowed
to touch communal food

12:54.271 --> 12:56.230
because his feet
smell like the street.

12:56.273 --> 12:58.667
I like when you measured my feet
at the store,

12:58.667 --> 13:00.451
Brian's girlfriend.

13:00.495 --> 13:03.280
Well, it...
it was my pleasure, Chris.

13:03.324 --> 13:06.544
I'm not actually sure
if my shoes fit right now.

13:06.631 --> 13:08.720
Um, could you do that thing

13:08.764 --> 13:12.159
where you push your thumb
on my big toe?

13:12.202 --> 13:14.770
Chris, you're within six years
of the same age

13:14.770 --> 13:17.425
as this kid you've never met
and have nothing in common with.

13:17.468 --> 13:18.992
Why don't you go up to your room

13:18.992 --> 13:20.907
and have
an awkward time together.

13:20.950 --> 13:23.431
Um, okay.
Want to go upstairs

13:23.474 --> 13:26.260
and accidentally break
one of my toys and I'll hit you?

13:26.260 --> 13:27.435
I guess.

13:28.740 --> 13:30.568
CHRIS:
Hey, don't touch that!

13:30.568 --> 13:31.787
-[thud]
-[slap]

13:31.874 --> 13:35.530
Mom!
He blocked my punch and hit me!

13:35.573 --> 13:37.184
I knew they'd get along.

13:37.227 --> 13:40.230
You know, Kyle and I actually
have to get going anyway,

13:40.274 --> 13:42.580
but thanks so much.

13:42.667 --> 13:44.365
Hey, Holly, before you go,

13:44.365 --> 13:46.541
settle an argument
between me and my wife.

13:46.584 --> 13:49.457
When measuring yourself,
what do you count as the base?

13:49.500 --> 13:51.807
-Peter.
-What? She measures stuff
for a living.

13:51.807 --> 13:55.245
Let me start
by saying I am taint inclusive.

13:55.289 --> 13:58.335
All right,
I like where this is heading.

13:58.379 --> 13:59.597
Well, thanks again for coming.

13:59.684 --> 14:01.164
Oh, hey, you know,
I was thinking

14:01.208 --> 14:03.514
we could take Kyle
to Bob's Funland on Saturday.

14:03.601 --> 14:05.821
Oh. Really?

14:05.821 --> 14:08.345
Yeah, I have to go there to buy
Adderall anyway, so I thought...

14:08.389 --> 14:11.479
Brian, stop.
I just... We can't go.

14:11.522 --> 14:14.525
-What? Why?
-Honestly, I've been thinking...

14:14.525 --> 14:16.310
STEWIE:
Uh-oh!

14:16.353 --> 14:17.789
Wh... W-What are you saying?

14:17.833 --> 14:20.270
Well, Brian, I'm still young.

14:20.314 --> 14:22.185
STEWIE:
Oh, she's saying you're not.

14:22.229 --> 14:24.274
And the truth is
I'd like to date other people.

14:24.318 --> 14:26.407
STEWIE [chuckles]:
Oh, nail, meet coffin.

14:26.494 --> 14:28.583
In fact, my old boyfriend
is single again,

14:28.626 --> 14:30.802
and he happens to be
a very selfless lover.

14:30.846 --> 14:31.891
STEWIE:
Dude, I told you.

14:31.934 --> 14:34.502
But i-if we break up,

14:34.545 --> 14:36.678
does that mean
I won't get to see Kyle, either?

14:38.549 --> 14:40.247
I guess not.

14:43.728 --> 14:45.556
I'm sorry, Brian.

14:45.643 --> 14:48.081
♪

14:55.740 --> 14:57.786
Touch my feet!

14:57.786 --> 15:00.441
-Touch my feet!
-Aah!

15:10.364 --> 15:12.148
[sighs]

15:13.454 --> 15:16.152
[sighs]

15:31.385 --> 15:34.997
-Oh. Hey, Stewie.
-Hey... you.

15:35.041 --> 15:37.695
-Feeling down?
-Yeah.

15:37.695 --> 15:39.915
Ah, don't worry about Holly.

15:40.002 --> 15:42.004
"There are other fish
in the sea"

15:42.048 --> 15:44.702
is what is usually said
at a time like this.

15:44.702 --> 15:47.792
-That's the thing.
It's not even Holly.
-Ugh. There's more?

15:47.836 --> 15:50.578
I mean, the person I actually
miss hanging out with is Kyle.

15:50.621 --> 15:52.362
We'd formed a real connection,

15:52.362 --> 15:54.974
and I sort of liked
being a father figure to him.

15:55.017 --> 15:57.802
That's... that's nice, Brian.

15:57.846 --> 15:59.804
Kyle and I
had actual fun together.

15:59.848 --> 16:01.589
I mean, most kids suck.

16:01.632 --> 16:03.852
They just want to sit around
and play Candy Land.

16:03.895 --> 16:06.724
-Yeah. Hell of a game.
-No, it's not.
Candy Landis terrible.

16:06.811 --> 16:07.987
There's not even any skill
to it.

16:08.030 --> 16:10.685
Uh, okay.
Um, you know what, Brian?

16:10.728 --> 16:12.295
You're hurt right now,

16:12.339 --> 16:14.602
and you're-you're saying things
that you don't mean.

16:14.645 --> 16:17.083
But listen,
if you miss Kyle that much,

16:17.126 --> 16:19.737
-you should go find him.
-Thanks. Maybe I will.

16:19.824 --> 16:20.825
Just hope
he doesn't want to play

16:20.869 --> 16:22.653
some stupid game like Go Fish.

16:22.697 --> 16:24.742
Go Fish is a thinking man's game

16:24.742 --> 16:26.527
of inquiry and consequence.
You know what?

16:26.614 --> 16:28.920
You know, I-I don't... I don't
have to explain myself to you.

16:28.964 --> 16:30.661
Go-go on.
Go find your kid.

16:36.450 --> 16:37.712
Damn it, what the hell
are we gonna do?

16:37.755 --> 16:40.106
-Joe's gonna be furious.
-Relax, Quagmire.

16:40.149 --> 16:41.890
From what I know
about car accidents,

16:41.933 --> 16:44.414
you can total your car,
completely walk away from it

16:44.458 --> 16:45.981
and still be Caitlyn Jenner.

16:45.981 --> 16:48.331
Besides, I'm pretty sure
I can pound this out.

16:51.856 --> 16:53.293
What the hell are you doing?

16:53.336 --> 16:56.165
-Crap, Joe's gonna kill us.
-Quagmire's right.

16:56.209 --> 16:58.776
Remember how upset he got
when they canceled Psych?

16:58.820 --> 17:00.126
[crying]

17:00.126 --> 17:02.302
Now who's gonna
expose charlatans

17:02.345 --> 17:05.653
by pretending to be psychic in
the greater Santa Barbara area?

17:10.745 --> 17:12.703
Oh, my God.

17:14.879 --> 17:16.751
What? What is this?

17:16.794 --> 17:19.014
Is this Ferris Bueller?

17:19.014 --> 17:21.712
Yeah, it's Ferris Bueller.

17:21.756 --> 17:24.193
Hundred percent
on  Ferris Bueller.

17:24.237 --> 17:27.153
Well, I'm glad
we got that settled.

17:27.196 --> 17:29.503
It's Fast Times
at Ridgemont High,you idiot!

17:29.546 --> 17:31.722
Joe, we all watched it
a week ago.

17:31.766 --> 17:35.204
Oh, yeah. You know, I enjoy
movies while I'm watching them,

17:35.248 --> 17:37.685
but the second they're over,
I can't remember a thing.

17:37.728 --> 17:39.034
Except Forrest Gump.

17:39.121 --> 17:41.036
[imitating Forrest Gump]:
"Try one of my candies.

17:41.036 --> 17:43.691
It'll tell you about life."

17:43.734 --> 17:46.128
[chuckles]
I can't forget that beauty.

17:46.172 --> 17:48.043
But what happened to my car?!

17:48.087 --> 17:49.610
We're really sorry, Joe.

17:49.697 --> 17:52.047
We took it without asking
and wrecked it.

17:52.091 --> 17:54.049
I like When Harry Met Sally...

17:54.049 --> 17:57.748
"I'll have the food
what made that lady came."

17:57.792 --> 17:59.620
You guys ruined my uncle's car.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.709
We're so sorry, Joe.

18:01.752 --> 18:04.842
-It's okay. I'm not mad.
-You're not?

18:04.929 --> 18:06.844
No.
In fact, uh,

18:06.888 --> 18:09.151
all I feel is relief.

18:09.195 --> 18:11.980
Caring for a car like that
requires round the clock effort.

18:12.023 --> 18:13.677
Do you know how much
of a pain in the ass that is?

18:13.721 --> 18:15.157
BONNIE:
Yes!

18:15.201 --> 18:16.202
I mean, cars are meant
to be driven,

18:16.202 --> 18:17.812
not kept in a garage.

18:17.855 --> 18:21.076
But it's too late now.
I mean, look at it.

18:21.076 --> 18:23.644
I couldn't drive this car
even if I wanted to.

18:24.993 --> 18:27.082
I'm not so sure about that.

18:27.126 --> 18:28.388
♪

18:28.431 --> 18:31.652
I'm doing it! I'm doing it!
This is awesome!

18:31.652 --> 18:33.088
I'm really d...
Oh,

18:33.088 --> 18:34.698
stop sign, Quagmire, stop sign!

18:34.742 --> 18:36.787
[tires screech]

18:36.831 --> 18:40.095
Joe's legs are, um...
colder than I expected.

18:40.139 --> 18:41.879
No blood.

18:49.017 --> 18:50.236
[indistinct chatter]

18:56.590 --> 18:57.721
[cheering]

19:00.681 --> 19:02.813
Brian, you made it!

19:02.857 --> 19:05.338
-Hey, buddy.
-What are you doing here?

19:05.338 --> 19:07.992
Holly, I was a terrible dad
with my own son,

19:08.036 --> 19:10.778
but I feel like I've made
a true connection with Kyle.

19:10.821 --> 19:12.345
Whoa, did you earn a ribbon?

19:12.432 --> 19:15.130
No, it's a bookmark
with a Bible verse on it.

19:15.130 --> 19:16.218
The priest was giving them out.

19:16.262 --> 19:18.829
Oh. Weird.
Well, how'd our car do?

19:18.873 --> 19:21.615
Second to last.
But I don't care.

19:21.658 --> 19:23.704
I had so much fun
making it with you.

19:23.791 --> 19:25.184
Me too, Kyle.

19:25.227 --> 19:27.621
[whistle blows]

19:27.664 --> 19:29.231
Okay, thanks
for a great event, everyone,

19:29.275 --> 19:30.928
but we need to clear out.

19:31.015 --> 19:33.148
There's a sex offender meeting
in ten minutes,

19:33.235 --> 19:35.150
and we can't have any overlap.

19:35.237 --> 19:37.848
Thank you, Brian.
It was sweet of you to come.

19:48.076 --> 19:52.776
Say, Brian, what are you doing
Saturday night?

19:58.869 --> 20:00.610
Hi. I'm almost ready.

20:00.654 --> 20:02.612
Great.

20:04.875 --> 20:08.096
-How you doing, champ?
-[knocking]

20:10.359 --> 20:12.405
Okay, Cliff and I should
be back by midnight.

20:12.405 --> 20:14.189
I left money for you two
to order a pizza.

20:14.233 --> 20:15.408
Sounds perfect.

20:16.931 --> 20:18.324
All right, Kyle,
what do you say you and me

20:18.367 --> 20:20.587
watch some Stranger Things?

20:20.630 --> 20:23.720
MORGAN FREEMAN:
Brian made Kyle
bread and butter,

20:23.764 --> 20:26.332
and kept the pizza money.

20:33.164 --> 20:36.124
Ich bin froh,
dass alles wieder normal ist.

20:36.167 --> 20:38.126
Tut mir leid wegen
deinem Auto, Joe.

20:38.126 --> 20:39.780
Es ist in Ordnung.

20:39.780 --> 20:41.999
Wo ist nun Jerome
mit den wiener?

20:42.043 --> 20:44.480
[giggles]
Wiener.

20:53.707 --> 20:54.795
Guten nacht,

20:54.795 --> 20:56.840
von das Disney Corporation.

21:34.704 --> 21:36.706
ANNOUNCER: Family Guy returns
with all new episodes.

21:36.793 --> 21:37.359
We're back.

21:37.490 --> 21:38.752
ANNOUNCER: Sundays on Fox.

21:38.926 --> 21:39.274
[upbeat music]